  "question": {
    "text": "A harbour lies in the direction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mi>o</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;south-west from a fort and at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> km from it. A ship sets out from the harbour at noon and sails due east at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> km/hour, then the time (in hours) in the evening at which the ship will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn></math> km from the fort is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be the position of the harbour and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> be of the fort. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/abs/2e37d884-3bdb-4cc0-a97a-4c17e211f646-Capture.JPG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Applying cosine formula in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>60</mn><mi>o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>900</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4900</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn></math>&nbsp;kms</p><p>Speed of ship =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> km/hr</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Time =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> hrs</p>",
